{"question_text": {"Oral Surgery-2": [{"id": "1", "question": "১) Following which is not the complication of flap surgery?", "option1": "ক) Flap tearing", "option2": "খ) Flap necrosis", "option3": "গ) Flap failure", "option4": "ঘ) Flap dehiscence", "answer": "3", "exp": ""}, {"id": "2", "question": "২) Which is the most common type of flap for surgical extraction?", "option1": "ক) Mucoperiosteal", "option2": "খ) Envelope type", "option3": "গ) Rhomboid flap", "option4": "ঘ) Triangular flap", "answer": "2", "exp": ""}, {"id": "3", "question": "৩) During hemostasis large vessels requires continuous pressure about-", "option1": "ক) 2-4 min", "option2": "খ) 5-7 min", "option3": "গ) 5-10 min", "option4": "ঘ) 15 min", "answer": "3", "exp": ""}, {"id": "4", "question": "৪) What may be the cause of dead space?", "option1": "ক) Teeth extraction", "option2": "খ) Accidental injury", "option3": "গ) Not suturing the wound in multiple layers", "option4": "ঘ) Spontaneously", "answer": "3", "exp": ""}, {"id": "5", "question": "৫) When the tooth is failed to errupt partially or completely in dental arch it is called a-", "option1": "ক) Unerupted tooth", "option2": "খ) Impacted tooth", "option3": "গ) Embedded tooth", "option4": "ঘ) Both b+c ", "answer": "4", "exp": ""}, {"id": "6", "question": "৬) What is not a local cause of impaction of tooth?", "option1": "ক) Ankylosed tooth", "option2": "খ) Dilacerated root", "option3": "গ) Ectopic tooth bud", "option4": "ঘ) Rickets", "answer": "4", "exp": ""}, {"id": "7", "question": "৭) What is not a winter’s line?", "option1": "ক) White", "option2": "খ) Amber", "option3": "গ) Red", "option4": "ঘ) Blue", "answer": "4", "exp": ""}, {"id": "8", "question": "৮) In minor oral surgery procedure which suture material is commonly used?", "option1": "ক) 2-0 silk", "option2": "খ) 3-0 silk", "option3": "গ) 2-0 catgut", "option4": "ঘ) 3-0 catgut", "answer": "2", "exp": ""}, {"id": "9", "question": "৯) During incision for molars which complication may happe